## Changes

+ [Added data types for `RaycastContext` enums and `Explosion.DestructionType`](https://github.com/apace100/calio/commit/88124f3027c6281c3e5594762d585b25fd8cac71)
* [Updated ordered resource listener registration system](https://github.com/apace100/calio/commit/a9ebe56c867e5fbd3106795911f3705e2d1ab812)
* [Made individual SerializableData fields accessible](https://github.com/apace100/calio/commit/4a0b46695aa1b1ef6e35bd079ce872c0aa98e37a)

## Update Notes for Developers

* If you used the ordered resource listener system before, it has now been migrated to a custom entrypoint in order to allow specifying `before` dependencies, instead of only `after`. It now also allows registering for `CLIENT_RESOURCES`, instead of only `SERVER_DATA`.

**Old (Calio <1.6.0)**
```java
public class SomeClass implements ModInitializer {
    @Override
    public void onInitialize() {
        OrderedResourceListeners.register(new MyDataLoader())
            .after(new Identifier("anothermod:cooldata"))
            .complete();
    }
}
```

**New (Calio >=1.6.0)**
`SomeClass.java`
```java
public class SomeClass implements OrderedResourceListenerInitializer {     
    @Override
    public void registerResourceListeners(OrderedResourceListenerManager manager) {
        manager.register(ResourceType.SERVER_DATA, new MyDataLoader())
            .after(new Identifier("anothermod:cooldata"))
            .complete();
    }
}
```
`fabric.mod.json`
```json
{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "id": "stuff",

    "entrypoints": {
        "calio:ordered-resource-listener": [
            "some.mod.package.SomeClass"
        ]
    }
}
```
----
* If you used a `DataObjectRegistry` with `readFromData` there has been a breaking change. You'll need to register the loader which reads the data yourself, either with the regular Vanilla system or using the aforementioned ordered resource listener entrypoint:

**Old (Calio <1.6.0)** (just calling `buildAndRegister` was enough - Calio handled registering the resource reload listener)
```java
public class SomeClass {
    public static final DataObjectRegistry<Thing> REGISTRY = new DataObjectRegistry.Builder<>(new Identifier("stuff:things"), Thing.class)
        .readFromData("things", true)
        .dataErrorHandler((id, exception) -> System.err.println("Failed to read thing " + id))
        .buildAndRegister();
}
```
**New (Calio >=1.6.0)** (Vanilla registration - not recommended)
```java
public class SomeClass implements ModInitializer {
    public static final DataObjectRegistry<Thing> REGISTRY = new DataObjectRegistry.Builder<>(new Identifier("stuff:things"), Thing.class)
        .readFromData("things", true)
        .dataErrorHandler((id, exception) -> System.err.println("Failed to read thing " + id))
        .buildAndRegister();

    @Override
    public void onInitialize() {
        // Needed since Calio 1.6.0, previously unnecessary
        ResourceManagerHelper.get(ResourceType.SERVER_DATA).registerReloadListener(REGISTRY.getLoader());
    }
}
```

**New (Calio >= 1.6.0)** (Ordered resource listener registration)
`SomeClass.java`
```java
public class SomeClass implements OrderedResourceListenerInitializer {
    public static final DataObjectRegistry<Thing> REGISTRY = new DataObjectRegistry.Builder<>(new Identifier("stuff:things"), Thing.class)
        .readFromData("things", true)
        .dataErrorHandler((id, exception) -> System.err.println("Failed to read thing " + id))
        .buildAndRegister();

    @Override
    public void registerResourceListeners(OrderedResourceListenerManager manager) {
        manager.register(ResourceType.SERVER_DATA, REGISTRY.getLoader()).complete();
    }
}
`fabric.mod.json`
```json
{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "id": "stuff",

    "entrypoints": {
        "calio:ordered-resource-listener": [
            "some.mod.package.SomeClass"
        ]
    }
}
```
